      "math_academy_id": "q-40561",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors  $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)(-1)+(2)(-1)+(3)(2)+(-4)(0)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6})≈{68.12}^{∘}.\n$$",
